#### 1. Global Navigation & System Telemetry Bar (Header)
- Header displaying system identity: `RIPON ROY // AUTONOMOUS AGENT FLOW ARCHITECT`
- Real-time simulated status indicators: `SYSTEM STATUS: PROCESSING...`, `ACTIVE AGENTS: 19/19`, `CPU: 73%`, `RAM: 62%`, `GPU: 89%`. Use horizontal progress bars for the hardware stats in cyan and magenta.

#### 2. Tiered Organizational Visual Grid / Tree
Organize all 19 agents into 5 interactive visual tiers, styled like a node-based flowchart with connecting lines or visual flow arrows:
- **Level 1 (Human Controller):** Ripon Roy (Chief of Editor) - Prominently framed at the top.
- **Level 2 (Executive Synthesis):** AI CEO.
- **Level 3 (C-Suite Execution):** AI CAIO, AI CFO, AI COO, AI CDO, AI CHRO.
- **Level 4 (Tactical Management):** AI Product Manager, Finance Manager, Operations Manager, Data Manager.
- **Level 5 (Specialized Fleet):** Workflow Orchestration, Supply & Operations Analytics, Data Quality, Skills Mapping, AI Ethics & Governance, AI Research Scientist, ML Engineer, MLOps Engineer, Data Engineer / Architect.

Each agent card must display:
- Role Title & Icon (Lucide SVG icons)
- Status Beacon (pulsing cyan dot for `ONLINE`)
- Action button: "Inspect Node" (opens Inspector Drawer).

#### 3. Slide-Out Holographic Inspector Drawer
Clicking any agent card opens a floating glass panel displaying:
- **Header:** Full Role Title and Operational Status.
- **System Prompt Block:** Monospace code block displaying the exact prompt from the schema (styled like a Python terminal input).
- **Mock Telemetry Metrics:** Floating line charts or node-graph visualizations (SVG or CSS mockups) with magenta and cyan nodes.

#### 4. Agentic Live Command Console (Bottom Panel)
- Terminal UI designed like a glowing touch console.
- Auto-scrolling simulated log feed illustrating hierarchical task propagation.
- Example log flow: `[RIPON ROY] > "Devise and implement a solution for optimal resource allocation"` → `[AI CEO] > Decomposing high-level goals...` 
- Interactive preset triggers allowing users to launch mock commands.

